{
  "_comment": [
    "Fake Artist words. Unlike content/prompts.json these are NOT pairs —",
    "everyone draws the same word and the fake knows they are the fake.",
    "",
    "The `theme` is the hint the fake receives when settings.themeHint is on.",
    "Authoring rule: a theme must be wide enough that naming it does not give",
    "the word away, and narrow enough that the fake can draw something that",
    "does not look instantly wrong. 'Buildings' for CASTLE works; 'Fortified",
    "medieval buildings' does not, and neither does 'Things'.",
    "",
    "Second rule: the word has to be *drawable in a few strokes*. A player gets",
    "one stroke per turn, so the whole picture is maybe 12-30 strokes between",
    "everyone. Abstract nouns are unplayable here — keep them concrete.",
    "",
    "`theme` is sent to the fake only, and only when the setting is on.",
    "The word itself reaches the crew through assignmentFor() and nowhere else,",
    "and becomes public in game:results."
  ],
